          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hángzhànlóu is built from háng 'to sail, to fly', 站 'a station' and lóu 'a building', all inherited from Middle Chinese, hang, treamH and luw (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'a boat' and the third as a building of several storeys."
